1
00:00:01,559 --> 00:00:03,080
[♪♪]

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:04,800
I'm Peppa Pig.

3
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,920
This is my little brother,
George.

4
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:08,119
[SNORTS]

5
00:00:08,119 --> 00:00:10,479
This is Mommy Pig.
[SNORTS]

6
00:00:10,479 --> 00:00:11,879
And this is Daddy Pig.

7
00:00:11,879 --> 00:00:13,320
[SNORTS]
[ALL LAUGH]

8
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:14,680
Peppa Pig.

9
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:15,920
[GRUNTS]

10
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:21,680
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

11
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:26,400
NARRATOR:
It is teatime.

12
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,720
And Mommy Pig has a surprise
for everyone.

13
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:31,479
[SNORTS]
Today is a day for pancakes.

14
00:00:31,479 --> 00:00:34,120
Pancakes. Delicious.

15
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:35,280
[GIGGLES AND SNORTS]

16
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:37,480
I love pancakes.
[LAUGHS]

17
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:39,960
[SNORTS]
[ALL LAUGH]

18
00:00:39,960 --> 00:00:41,680
Everyone loves pancakes.

19
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:44,720
I'm the expert at flipping
the pancakes over.

20
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,000
Leave that to me.

21
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:47,720
Are you sure,
Daddy Pig?

22
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:49,320
Last time you got
a bit grumpy

23
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:51,640
when you dropped the pancake
on the floor.

24
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:53,440
I did not get grumpy.

25
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:56,239
There was a problem
with the frying pan.

26
00:00:56,239 --> 00:00:58,080
[ALL LAUGH]

27
00:00:58,080 --> 00:01:01,720
Mommy, can we help
make the pancakes? Please?

28
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:03,320
[SNORTS]
Yes.

29
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:05,519
You can help me
make the batter.

30
00:01:05,519 --> 00:01:09,039
First I put some flour
in the bowl.

31
00:01:09,039 --> 00:01:10,679
BOTH:
Ooh.

32
00:01:10,679 --> 00:01:13,200
MOMMY PIG:
Now I add an egg.

33
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:16,440
Now the milk.

34
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:19,880
And I give it all
a stir.

35
00:01:20,759 --> 00:01:22,720
[SNORTS]
Mommy, can I stir?

36
00:01:22,720 --> 00:01:24,399
Yes, of course, Peppa.

37
00:01:24,399 --> 00:01:26,800
Peppa loves stirring.

38
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:28,039
[SNORTS]

39
00:01:28,039 --> 00:01:29,759
George wants to stir
as well.

40
00:01:29,759 --> 00:01:31,240
[SNICKERS]

41
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:35,119
No, George, like this.

42
00:01:35,119 --> 00:01:36,960
[BOTH LAUGH]

43
00:01:38,160 --> 00:01:40,160
Okay, that's enough
stirring.

44
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:43,320
You two sit at the table
while I cook the pancakes.

45
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:44,920
[GAS HISSES]

46
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:49,960
[SIZZLING]

47
00:01:52,199 --> 00:01:55,160
Mommy Pig is going
to flip the pancake over.

48
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:58,240
Hooray!
[ALL LAUGH]

49
00:01:58,240 --> 00:02:00,440
You could flip it higher,
Mommy Pig.

50
00:02:00,440 --> 00:02:03,160
You can show us how
when you flip your own pancake,

51
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:04,759
Daddy Pig.

52
00:02:04,759 --> 00:02:07,119
This first pancake
is for George.

53
00:02:07,119 --> 00:02:10,000
Mommy Pig pours a little syrup
on George's pancake.

54
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:13,079
[SMACKS LIPS AND SNORTS]

55
00:02:13,079 --> 00:02:14,840
Delicious.

56
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:18,840
This pancake is for Peppa.

57
00:02:19,799 --> 00:02:21,160
PEPPA:
Hooray!

58
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:22,480
[ALL CHUCKLE]

59
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:25,600
Hmm. You could flip it higher,
Mommy Pig.

60
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:27,799
MOMMY PIG:
You will get a chance to show me

61
00:02:27,799 --> 00:02:30,079
when you flip you own pancake,
Daddy Pig.

62
00:02:30,079 --> 00:02:31,799
Syrup, please.

63
00:02:34,079 --> 00:02:36,120
[LIPS SMACK]

64
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:37,760
Mmm, delicious.

65
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:39,160
[LAUGHS]

66
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:42,760
This pancake
is for Mommy Pig.

67
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:45,200
PEPPA:
Hooray!

68
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:46,799
[ALL LAUGH]

69
00:02:46,799 --> 00:02:49,799
You still aren't flipping them
high enough, Mommy Pig.

70
00:02:49,799 --> 00:02:52,320
The next pancake is yours,
Daddy Pig.

71
00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:55,040
So now you can show us
how it should be done.

72
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:58,280
[SMACKS LIPS]

73
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:00,519
Delicious.

74
00:03:00,519 --> 00:03:01,880
[LAUGHS AND SNORTS]

75
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:04,679
Is everyone watching?

76
00:03:04,679 --> 00:03:08,000
The secret of making
a good pancake

77
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,799
is to flip it high
into the air.

78
00:03:11,799 --> 00:03:15,480
One, two, three...

79
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:16,920
hoopla!

80
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,760
[MOMMY PIG GASPS]

81
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:20,959
[GIGGLES]

82
00:03:20,959 --> 00:03:22,959
Silly Daddy.
Oh.

83
00:03:22,959 --> 00:03:25,880
Maybe that was just
a bit too high.

84
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:28,920
Oh, what a shame.
That was the last pancake.

85
00:03:28,920 --> 00:03:31,560
It should be a simple matter
to get it down.

86
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:36,760
Oh, dear. Daddy Pig cannot
reach his pancake.

87
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:38,720
MOMMY PIG:
Don't worry, Daddy Pig.

88
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:40,880
I think I know a way
to get it down.

89
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:42,799
Let's go upstairs,
children.

90
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:45,600
[GIGGLING]
This way.

91
00:03:46,799 --> 00:03:49,399
What is Mommy Pig
planning to do?

92
00:03:49,399 --> 00:03:50,679
On the count of three,

93
00:03:50,679 --> 00:03:53,679
we all have to start jumping
up and down.

94
00:03:53,679 --> 00:03:55,920
One, two, three.

95
00:03:55,920 --> 00:03:58,399
Jump!
[ALL LAUGH]

96
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:02,160
[THUDDING]

97
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:04,519
What are they doing?

98
00:04:04,519 --> 00:04:07,880
[♪♪]

99
00:04:12,399 --> 00:04:13,760
It worked.

100
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:15,959
Now Daddy Pig
has his pancake.

101
00:04:15,959 --> 00:04:18,000
Daddy has a pancake
on his head.

102
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,959
[ALL LAUGH]
Hmm.

103
00:04:20,959 --> 00:04:23,080
Syrup on your pancake,
Daddy Pig?

104
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:24,719
Yes, please.

105
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:27,920
[GIGGLING]

106
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:31,400
One, two, three...

107
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:32,960
hoopla!

108
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:34,800
Mmm.

109
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:39,240
Delicious.

110
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:41,280
[ALL LAUGH]

111
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:42,800
Silly Daddy.

112
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:53,280
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

113
00:04:56,039 --> 00:04:59,520
NARRATOR:
Mommy Pig and Daddy Pig
are going out for the evening.

114
00:04:59,520 --> 00:05:02,320
Granny Pig and Grandpa Pig
are going to babysit.

115
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:04,919
Granny Pig! Grandpa Pig!

116
00:05:04,919 --> 00:05:07,520
[MISPRONOUNCES]
Granny Pig! Grandpa Pig!

117
00:05:07,520 --> 00:05:09,560
Hello, my little ones.

118
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:11,240
Hello.

119
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:13,599
Peppa, George,
into your beds, quick.

120
00:05:13,599 --> 00:05:15,760
[BOTH GIGGLE]

121
00:05:15,760 --> 00:05:18,000
Good night,
my little piggies.

122
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,880
Good night. Sleep tight.

123
00:05:19,880 --> 00:05:23,159
Good night, Mommy.
Good night, Daddy.

124
00:05:23,159 --> 00:05:24,320
[SNORTS]

125
00:05:24,320 --> 00:05:26,520
What little darlings.

126
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:28,560
Now go to sleep
quickly.

127
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:29,840
Yes, Mommy.

128
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:31,960
So well-behaved.

129
00:05:34,159 --> 00:05:37,359
Mommy Pig and Daddy Pig are
leaving for their evening out.

130
00:05:37,359 --> 00:05:39,080
[ENGINE STARTS]

131
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,400
Peppa and George
are so good.

132
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:54,680
They just fell asleep
when Mommy Pig told them to.

133
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:57,760
[SNORTS]
This babysitting is easy.

134
00:06:00,919 --> 00:06:03,640
George? George?

135
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:05,359
Are you awake?

136
00:06:05,359 --> 00:06:06,640
[SNORTS]

137
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:08,359
[GIGGLES]

138
00:06:14,400 --> 00:06:16,400
Shh!

139
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:19,240
[BOTH SNICKER]

140
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:21,240
[LOUD THUMPING]

141
00:06:24,159 --> 00:06:26,640
What strange noises.

142
00:06:26,640 --> 00:06:29,880
I wonder if we should
check upstairs.

143
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:32,640
[BOTH LAUGHING
AND SNORTING]

144
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:40,039
Peppa, George.

145
00:06:40,039 --> 00:06:42,000
Are you awake?

146
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:47,960
Well, I never.

147
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:49,599
Fast asleep.

148
00:06:49,599 --> 00:06:55,440
So it wasn't Peppa and George
making all that noise.

149
00:07:01,760 --> 00:07:05,039
[SNORTS]
I can't hear anything.

150
00:07:05,039 --> 00:07:07,400
I think they really have
fallen asleep.

151
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:10,960
[SNORTS]
Let's watch some television.

152
00:07:10,960 --> 00:07:12,440
MAN [OVER TV]:
Gardening.

153
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:14,919
Today, we are talking
about roses.

154
00:07:14,919 --> 00:07:18,560
Oh, I love gardening
programs.

155
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:22,120
The Kiftsgate is a particularly
thorny rose.

156
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:24,960
To prune it,

157
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:26,880
start by lopping off
the head

158
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:30,320
and then snip away
the budding shoots.

159
00:07:30,320 --> 00:07:31,960
Granny Pig?

160
00:07:31,960 --> 00:07:33,560
GRANNY PIG:
Peppa? George?

161
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:35,719
You should be
in bed asleep.

162
00:07:35,719 --> 00:07:38,120
George and I
aren't sleepy at all.

163
00:07:38,120 --> 00:07:41,159
[SNORTS]
Can we watch TV with you?

164
00:07:41,159 --> 00:07:43,520
Well, I suppose
watching a little TV

165
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:44,960
might make you sleepy.

166
00:07:44,960 --> 00:07:46,560
Hooray!
[GIGGLES]

167
00:07:47,760 --> 00:07:50,080
Icelandic Roses
are a rare treat

168
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:52,400
for the discerning
horticulturist,

169
00:07:52,400 --> 00:07:55,960
but they are prone to lobbing
in temperate habitats.

170
00:07:55,960 --> 00:07:57,080
[YAWNS]

171
00:07:57,080 --> 00:07:59,280
This program
is very boring.

172
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:00,440
[YAWNS]

173
00:08:00,440 --> 00:08:02,760
Grandpa Pig,
can you play that game

174
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:05,479
where you throw us up
and catch us?

175
00:08:05,479 --> 00:08:08,880
Okay, but just one turn each.

176
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:10,039
[GIGGLES]

177
00:08:10,039 --> 00:08:11,400
Whee!
Whee!

178
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:12,640
[LAUGHS]

179
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:14,719
Oh, you seem heavier
than before.

180
00:08:14,719 --> 00:08:15,919
[SNORTING]

181
00:08:15,919 --> 00:08:17,120
[LAUGHS]

182
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:19,359
Now it's George's turn.

183
00:08:19,359 --> 00:08:20,679
Whee!
Whee!

184
00:08:20,679 --> 00:08:22,000
[BOTH LAUGH]

185
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:23,320
My turn.

186
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:24,679
Whee!
Whee!

187
00:08:24,679 --> 00:08:27,200
Whew.
Higher, higher.

188
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:28,440
[PANTING]
Whee!

189
00:08:28,440 --> 00:08:31,000
Maybe Grandpa Pig
is a bit tired.

190
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:35,079
I know. Granny Pig,
let's play catch.

191
00:08:35,079 --> 00:08:36,280
Uh...

192
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:37,760
[GIGGLES]
You're it.

193
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:39,400
Catch us if you can.

194
00:08:39,400 --> 00:08:40,640
[LAUGHS]

195
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:42,000
PEPPA:
Can't catch me.

196
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,079
GRANNY PIG:
I'm going to catch you.

197
00:08:44,079 --> 00:08:46,040
[ALL LAUGHING]

198
00:08:52,319 --> 00:08:55,079
NARRATOR:
Mommy Pig and Daddy Pig
are back home.

199
00:08:55,079 --> 00:08:57,880
I hope our little piggies
are asleep.

200
00:08:57,880 --> 00:08:59,600
[TELEVISION STATIC CRACKLING]

201
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:01,800
Hello? Anyone here?

202
00:09:01,800 --> 00:09:03,600
[ALL SNORING]

203
00:09:04,800 --> 00:09:06,280
[DADDY PIG LAUGHS]

204
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:08,199
The little piggies
are asleep.

205
00:09:08,199 --> 00:09:10,439
And so are
the big piggies.

206
00:09:10,439 --> 00:09:12,600
[BOTH LAUGH]

207
00:09:21,199 --> 00:09:24,640
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

208
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:27,800
NARRATOR:
Peppa is going to her first
ballet lesson.

209
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:30,319
This is Madame Gazelle,
the ballet teacher.

210
00:09:30,319 --> 00:09:33,079
Oh, you must be
young Peppa.

211
00:09:33,079 --> 00:09:36,800
I am Madame Gazelle.

212
00:09:39,079 --> 00:09:40,959
Hello, Madame.

213
00:09:42,199 --> 00:09:44,360
Aww, so sweet.

214
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:49,800
Welcome to your first lesson
of the ballet.

215
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:51,000
[GIGGLES]

216
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,439
I'll pick you up later.

217
00:09:52,439 --> 00:09:55,120
Bye-bye.
Enjoy yourself.

218
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:57,480
[ALL LAUGHING] 
Here are Peppa's friends,

219
00:09:57,480 --> 00:09:59,720
Candy Cat, Suzy Sheep,
Danny Dog,

220
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:02,800
Rebecca Rabbit
and Pedro Pony.

221
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:08,480
Children, today we have
a new pupil: Peppa Pig.

222
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:10,640
Now, Peppa, run and join
your friends.

223
00:10:10,640 --> 00:10:12,560
[SNORTS AND LAUGHS]

224
00:10:12,560 --> 00:10:15,000
Hello, everyone.
ALL: Hello, Peppa.

225
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,720
[ALL MAKING ANIMAL NOISES]

226
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:19,079
GAZELLE:
Children.

227
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:22,959
We begin with demi-plié.

228
00:10:22,959 --> 00:10:25,480
[LOW-TEMPO PIANO MUSIC PLAYS]

229
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:29,560
Demi-plié.

230
00:10:34,439 --> 00:10:36,680
Now a little jump.

231
00:10:36,680 --> 00:10:39,000
Petit jeté.

232
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:46,280
With grace and beauty.

233
00:10:46,280 --> 00:10:48,360
Petit jeté.

234
00:10:49,839 --> 00:10:52,319
Grace and beauty.

235
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:02,640
Petit jeté.

236
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:05,920
Grace and beauty.

237
00:11:07,280 --> 00:11:08,640
[GIGGLES]

238
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:11,079
The ballet lesson
is a lot of fun.

239
00:11:11,079 --> 00:11:13,040
Raise you arms.

240
00:11:15,959 --> 00:11:19,959
Imagine that you are
beautiful swans.

241
00:11:28,520 --> 00:11:32,240
And what noise do you think
a swan might make?

242
00:11:32,240 --> 00:11:35,839
[ALL MAKING ANIMAL SOUNDS]

243
00:11:35,839 --> 00:11:38,880
Oh!
[ALL CHATTER]

244
00:11:38,880 --> 00:11:41,560
Grace and beauty.

245
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:43,240
Peppa loves dancing.

246
00:11:43,240 --> 00:11:44,920
Everyone loves dancing.

247
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:47,600
[TOLLING]

248
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:50,520
[CHILDREN LAUGHING]

249
00:11:52,439 --> 00:11:53,839
Mommy. Mommy.

250
00:11:53,839 --> 00:11:56,160
[SNORTS]
We all danced as swans.

251
00:11:56,160 --> 00:11:58,680
Peppa did very well.

252
00:11:58,680 --> 00:12:02,560
I had to dance beautifully
and gracefully.

253
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:04,120
That's lovely.

254
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:06,719
Can I show you
how I did it?

255
00:12:06,719 --> 00:12:08,199
Let's get home first.

256
00:12:08,199 --> 00:12:11,719
Then you can show Daddy Pig
and George and me.

257
00:12:11,719 --> 00:12:13,040
[ENGINE STARTS]

258
00:12:13,040 --> 00:12:15,160
Bye-bye.

259
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:18,760
[CAR HORN BLARES]

260
00:12:18,760 --> 00:12:20,719
Peppa and Mommy Pig are home.

261
00:12:22,040 --> 00:12:23,719
Daddy. George.

262
00:12:23,719 --> 00:12:26,600
I'm going to show you
how to do ballet.

263
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:28,000
Is it difficult?

264
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,959
It was easy for me.

265
00:12:29,959 --> 00:12:34,079
But you, George and Mommy
will find it very hard.

266
00:12:34,079 --> 00:12:35,280
[SNORTS]

267
00:12:35,280 --> 00:12:37,079
First, we need music.

268
00:12:37,079 --> 00:12:38,640
[GENTLE PIANO MUSIC PLAYS]

269
00:12:38,640 --> 00:12:42,199
Good. Now, George,
Daddy and Mommy,

270
00:12:42,199 --> 00:12:44,880
you must copy
what I do.

271
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:47,319
Madame Gazelle
used funny words.

272
00:12:47,319 --> 00:12:52,120
But really it's just bending
your knees and jumping.

273
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:53,480
Ah.

274
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:55,360
The petit jeté.

275
00:12:55,360 --> 00:12:58,360
Daddy! You know the funny words.

276
00:12:58,360 --> 00:12:59,760
[LAUGHS]
Mommy Pig and I

277
00:12:59,760 --> 00:13:02,079
used to be quite good
at ballet.

278
00:13:05,680 --> 00:13:07,439
Do be careful,
Daddy Pig.

279
00:13:07,439 --> 00:13:08,680
[LAUGHS AND SNORTS]

280
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:11,599
Our favorite was
the pas de deux.

281
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:18,800
Hoopla!

282
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:20,439
Oof!
Aah!

283
00:13:20,439 --> 00:13:23,439
That wasn't quite
how I remembered it.

284
00:13:23,439 --> 00:13:25,480
[SNICKERS]

285
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:28,480
Silly Daddy Pig.

286
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:31,640
Maybe we should leave the ballet
to Peppa.

287
00:13:31,640 --> 00:13:35,280
Yes, I am the best at it.

288
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:41,959
I am a beautiful swan.

289
00:13:41,959 --> 00:13:43,480
[SNORTS]

290
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:45,360
[ALL LAUGH]

291
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:53,040
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

292
00:13:55,640 --> 00:13:57,040
[BOTH GIGGLING]

293
00:13:57,040 --> 00:13:59,040
NARRATOR:
It is a lovely, sunny day.

294
00:13:59,040 --> 00:14:01,800
Peppa and George
are having a picnic.

295
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:04,719
Here's some orange juice
for you, Teddy.

296
00:14:04,719 --> 00:14:06,400
What do you say?

297
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:08,839
Thank you very much,
Peppa.

298
00:14:08,839 --> 00:14:11,400
You are very
welcome, Teddy.

299
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:14,719
Here's some orange juice
for you, Mr. Dinosaur.

300
00:14:14,719 --> 00:14:16,760
And what do you say?

301
00:14:16,760 --> 00:14:18,319
Grr!

302
00:14:18,319 --> 00:14:21,199
You are very welcome,
Mr. Dinosaur.

303
00:14:21,199 --> 00:14:22,800
[LAUGHS AND SNORTS]

304
00:14:22,800 --> 00:14:25,520
Would Teddy or Mr. Dinosaur
like a cookie?

305
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:27,760
We're not very hungry.

306
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:30,800
So Peppa and George can eat
all the cookies.

307
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:32,880
Thank you, Teddy.

308
00:14:36,719 --> 00:14:38,479
[BOTH LAUGH]

309
00:14:38,479 --> 00:14:40,280
[THUNDER RUMBLES]

310
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:42,640
What is that
strange noise?

311
00:14:44,199 --> 00:14:45,959
Peppa! George!

312
00:14:45,959 --> 00:14:48,520
Quick, come inside
the house.

313
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:52,040
Mommy, there was
a loud bang sound.

314
00:14:52,040 --> 00:14:53,959
It's thunder, Peppa.

315
00:14:53,959 --> 00:14:58,000
It means there will be a
thunderstorm with lots of rain.

316
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:01,000
Quick. Into the house
before the rain starts.

317
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,079
[LAUGHS]
No need to panic.

318
00:15:03,079 --> 00:15:07,040
The rain is still
a long way off.

319
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:09,360
The sky is getting
darker and darker.

320
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:11,839
There is going
to be a thunderstorm.

321
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:16,880
Peppa, George,

322
00:15:16,880 --> 00:15:19,479
did you bring all your toys
in from the garden?

323
00:15:19,479 --> 00:15:21,240
Dinosaur.

324
00:15:21,240 --> 00:15:23,520
MOMMY PIG:
Good, Mr. Dinosaur is safe.

325
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:26,079
Teddy! I left Teddy
in the garden.

326
00:15:26,079 --> 00:15:27,360
He'll get wet.

327
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:29,199
DADDY PIG:
Don't worry, Peppa.

328
00:15:29,199 --> 00:15:31,040
Daddy Pig will rescue Teddy.

329
00:15:31,040 --> 00:15:34,240
You'd better hurry, Daddy Pig.
It's just about to rain.

330
00:15:34,240 --> 00:15:36,520
I know all about
thunderstorms.

331
00:15:36,520 --> 00:15:38,640
It won't rain for ages.

332
00:15:38,640 --> 00:15:41,000
[CHUCKLES AND SNORTS]

333
00:15:42,959 --> 00:15:44,400
As I thought.

334
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:46,959
Plenty of time
before it rains.

335
00:15:49,439 --> 00:15:51,040
[SHUDDERING]

336
00:15:53,079 --> 00:15:55,640
[PANTING]

337
00:15:55,640 --> 00:15:57,560
Poor Teddy.

338
00:15:57,560 --> 00:15:59,560
He's soaking wet.

339
00:15:59,560 --> 00:16:01,560
Yes, poor Teddy.

340
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:02,920
Let's get him dry.

341
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:04,560
Poor Teddy.

342
00:16:04,560 --> 00:16:06,520
[SHIVERING]

343
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:08,719
There you are, Teddy.
All dry.

344
00:16:08,719 --> 00:16:09,959
[BOTH LAUGH]

345
00:16:09,959 --> 00:16:11,319
[SNEEZES]

346
00:16:11,319 --> 00:16:13,439
What about poor Daddy?

347
00:16:13,439 --> 00:16:15,560
I'm soaking wet too.

348
00:16:15,560 --> 00:16:17,839
Oh. Sorry, Daddy Pig.

349
00:16:17,839 --> 00:16:19,359
Let's get you dry.

350
00:16:19,359 --> 00:16:21,319
[ALL LAUGH]

351
00:16:23,359 --> 00:16:25,160
There you are,
Daddy Pig.

352
00:16:25,160 --> 00:16:26,959
Nice and dry.
[SNORTS]

353
00:16:26,959 --> 00:16:28,880
Hmm.

354
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:31,079
Oh!

355
00:16:31,079 --> 00:16:34,520
The rain is coming
in the house.

356
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:39,240
The floor is getting wet.

357
00:16:39,240 --> 00:16:40,439
Oh, dear.

358
00:16:40,439 --> 00:16:42,160
What can we do,
Daddy Pig?

359
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:43,800
Don't worry.

360
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:47,199
Daddy Pig is using a bucket
to catch the drips.

361
00:16:47,199 --> 00:16:49,599
MOMMY PIG:
Well done, Daddy Pig.

362
00:16:49,599 --> 00:16:52,120
Easy as pie.

363
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:54,000
Eh? What?

364
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:55,479
[GASPS]

365
00:16:55,479 --> 00:16:59,240
Quick, find something else
to catch the water.

366
00:17:01,760 --> 00:17:03,959
Well done, Peppa.

367
00:17:03,959 --> 00:17:06,040
Easy as pie.

368
00:17:06,040 --> 00:17:07,560
[ALL LAUGH]

369
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:09,480
[THUNDER CRASHES]

370
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:13,359
Aah! Mommy, the thunder bangs
are very loud.

371
00:17:13,359 --> 00:17:16,960
It's okay, children.
Don't be frightened.

372
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:19,639
Let's count between
each flash and bang.

373
00:17:19,639 --> 00:17:21,119
The higher
we can count,

374
00:17:21,119 --> 00:17:23,480
the further away
the thunderstorm is.

375
00:17:23,480 --> 00:17:28,280
One, two, three...

376
00:17:28,280 --> 00:17:30,480
[THUNDER CRASHES]

377
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:31,720
[SNORTS]

378
00:17:31,720 --> 00:17:33,440
That's three.

379
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:37,720
ALL:
One, two, three,

380
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:40,639
four, five...

381
00:17:40,639 --> 00:17:42,600
[THUNDER CRASHES]

382
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:44,200
That's five.

383
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:46,879
The thunderstorm
is going away.

384
00:17:46,879 --> 00:17:49,280
[BIRDS SINGING]

385
00:17:49,280 --> 00:17:51,480
[SNORTS]
The thunderstorm is over.

386
00:17:51,480 --> 00:17:53,840
ALL:
Hooray!

387
00:17:53,840 --> 00:17:57,320
The thunderstorm has filled
the garden with muddy puddles.

388
00:17:57,320 --> 00:17:59,040
[BOTH LAUGHING]

389
00:17:59,040 --> 00:18:01,800
Peppa loves jumping
up and down in muddy puddles.

390
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:03,440
[ALL LAUGH]

391
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:06,399
Everyone loves jumping
up and down in muddy puddles.

392
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:09,800
I love thunderstorms.

393
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:12,360
They make muddy puddles.

394
00:18:12,360 --> 00:18:14,879
Splish-splash,
splosh-splish.

395
00:18:14,879 --> 00:18:16,639
[ALL LAUGHING]

396
00:18:19,919 --> 00:18:22,040
[PEPPA GIGGLING]

397
00:18:22,040 --> 00:18:23,720
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

398
00:18:23,720 --> 00:18:26,800
[SNORTS AND LAUGHS]

399
00:18:26,800 --> 00:18:28,560
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

400
00:18:28,560 --> 00:18:31,200
[SNORTS AND LAUGHS]

401
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:32,679
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

402
00:18:32,679 --> 00:18:34,320
[SNORTS AND LAUGHS]

